The complete raw strace contains 8,544 futex calls; all unfinished/resumed calls paired and there were zero pending or unparsed records. Of 2,481 successful FUTEX_WAIT calls and 2,478 positive FUTEX_WAKE calls, the raw-pipe output writer TID 863811 made 598 successful waits of at least 1 ms. Each of those 598 waits (592 at least 10 ms) had a positive same-address FUTEX_WAKE syscall from FFmpeg leader TID 863769 temporally inside the writer wait interval. This is a temporal association, not kernel-confirmed waiter identity: FUTEX_WAKE does not report which waiter it awakened, and a concurrent same-address waiter could have been selected. Pairs split evenly across futex addresses 0x55a0026bb0 and 0x55a0026bb4 (299 each); median wake-to-wait-completion time was 0.201 ms. All 598 had a temporal same-address positive wake association; this is not kernel-confirmed waiter identity.

